\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr/12-Yr Low -2: Selling Versus Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 202 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 04:35\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar remains weaker at midsession Wednesday after slumping to a fresh 12-year low against the U.S. dollar late morning, amid selling against the yen. \par \par \uc2  "The break down of Y82.50" saw stop-loss sell orders triggered, according to one domestic bank dealer, which then drove the Australian dollar on down to a Y81.99 low. \par \par \uc2  The selling also saw the Australian dollar slide under US$0.5850 to US$0.5833, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lowest level reached since July 1986. \par \par \uc2  There has been some rumbling about possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar Wednesday; however, no dealers have actually cited any \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying, and according to the domestic bank dealer, "the rumors are probably just that, rumors." \par \par \uc2  At 0225 GMT, the Australian dollar is quoted at US$0.5844, down nearly one-and-a-half U.S. cents from US$0.5983 late in Sydney Tuesday. It also is at Y82.17, below Y84.07 Tuesday, while the trade-weighted index has fallen to 54.7 from 55.7. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 10-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0235GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6a04y3c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
