\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Weaker Early, Slides To New Near 12-Yr Low \b0\par\par\uc2 377 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juni 1998\par 00:21\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar fell to a fresh near 12-year low vs. the U.S. dollar overnight, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  not helped by overnight gold and commodity price weakness. \par \par \uc2  At 2205 GMT, the Australian dollar is quoted at US$0.5923, below US$0.5983 locally late Tuesday. It also is at Y83.10, below Y84.07 Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar extended recent losses to US$0.5918 overnight, its lowest level reached since July 1986. One domestic bank dealer says the move was fueled by stop-loss selling on the break of US$0.5950. \par \par \uc2  Also pressuring the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight was a sharp drop in the gold price following comments from European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Wim Duisenberg, indicating gold would make up 10% to 15% of ECB reserves, slightly below market expectations of gold reserves of more than 15%. The metal was last quoted at US$293.65/oz, down from US$295.55/oz late in Sydney Tuesday, and well off an overnight peak of US$299.05/oz. \par \par \uc2  Commodity prices also fell overnight, the KR-CRB index of commodity prices closing down 1.82 points at 211.51. \par \par \uc2  Adding to pressure on the Australian dollar were comments from Standard & Poor's analyst, David Beers, in a telephone interview with Dow Jones Newswires overnight, that while the weaker Australian dollar doesn't have direct relevance to Australia's sovereign debt rating, it could exert downward pressure on rating of Australian corporates. \par \par \uc2  Over the local trading day, the dealer says the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  should find resistance around US$0.5940/US$0.5950 and support near US$0.5900, unless the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in which case the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could rally back toward US$0.5980-US$0.6000. \par \par \uc2  Over the medium term, the dealer suggests the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could target a retest of its all-time low at US$0.5717, touched in July 1986. He says the only things that might stand in the way are an increase in domestic interest rates, or Bank of Japan \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to stem the yen's downward trend. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 09-06-98 \par \par \uc2  2221GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6904xvy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
