\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Bond Mkt Rout Signals Retail Rates To Rise \b0\par\par\uc2  By Iain McDonald \par \uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1998\par 09:16\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--A rout of Australia's bond market Tuesday is a signal that the country has seen the last of falling interest rates, with some retail and corporate lending rates set to increase in coming weeks. \par \par \uc2  Bond yields rose sharply to their highest level in five months on fears that the Reserve Bank of Australia may resort to raising interest rates to support the sagging Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has fallen sharply over the past week, dragged down by the yen's slump against the U.S. dollar, and concerns about the impact Asia's economic woes will have on Australia. The Australian dollar touched a new 12-year low of US$0.5954 overnight after falling below US$0.6000 on Monday, despite rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  While the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  is concerned about the slide in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the knock-on effect that would have on inflation via higher import prices, few expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to hike interest rates immediately. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, some retail and corporate lending rates will rise anyway, if bond yields maintain their higher levels. \par \par \uc2  At the top of the hit list are fixed home-loan rates, traditionally determined by bond yields. Those fixed rates have only recently been cut by many banks in response to a bond market rally that ended abruptly in late May. \par \par \uc2  One of the first to move in the opposite direction could be Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd. (ANZ). ANZ, one of Australia's four biggest banks, is currently reviewing its rates and expects to make an announcement on its fixed home-loan rates "towards the end of the week," says head of group media relations, Paul Edwards. \par \par \uc2  "There is considerable upward pressure" on short-end fixed rates, such as one- and two-year fixed rates, Edwards said. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 09-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0716GMT \par \par \uc2  1139 4203 62553 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6904wpm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
