\par\par \b \uc2  Australia/Costello/A$ -4: Refers To Macfarlane Rate Comments \b0\par\par\uc2 215 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1998\par 02:25\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  When asked whether he supported \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the falling \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the past few days, Costello said: "The Reserve Bank has the full backing of the Australian government." \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is rumored to have bought up to A$3 billion in \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets to stem the dollar's slide. \par \par \uc2  When asked whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  might be forced to increase its overnight cash rate, which stands at 5%, to help support the Australian dollar, Costello declined to speculate on the direction of interest rates. \par \par \uc2  The treasurer said monetary policy settings are the responsibility of the independent Reserve Bank. \par \par \uc2  "In relation to interest rates, I've always said to you, and I continue to say to you, I've never given a forward indication in relation to interest rates, never given an indication when they go up, or when the go down," he said. \par \par \uc2  However Costello indicated the government believes an interest rate cut is unlikely, suggesting people refer to comments made last week by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Ian Macfarlane on London. \par \par \uc2  Macfarlane said a rate cut was "very unlikely." \par \par \uc2  -By Benjamin Pedley; 612-6208-0901; bpedley@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0025GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6904vvo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*