\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dollar Weaker Early, But Off Monday's Lows \b0\par\par\uc2 239 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1998\par 00:13\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar is weaker early Tuesday, after sliding under key psychological support at US$0.6000 in dealings Monday. \par \par \uc2  At 2200 GMT, the Australian dollar is quoted at US$0.5974, down from US$0.6057 locally late Friday. It also is at Y84.27, below Y84.41 Friday. Australian markets were closed Monday for a public holiday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar fell to a fresh, near 12-year low at US$0.5954 during the Asian trading day Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finding little support from "strong" rumors of further Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early New Zealand trading, according to dealers. They estimate the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought around A$250 million Monday, following the rumored A$2 billion to A$3 billion thought to have been bought by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last Thursday and Friday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar managed to rally back from its lows to a US$0.6023 peak in New York overnight, however, the move in line with a jump in the gold price after aggressive buying by one player prompted a bout of short-covering, dealers say. The metal was last quoted at US$296.95/oz, well up from a US$289.35/oz overnight low, and above US$293.00/oz seen locally late Friday. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 08-06-98 \par \par \uc2  2213GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6804vo6\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichg