\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Bond Prices Set To Open Lower, Focus On Weak A$ \b0\par\par\uc2 399 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Juni 1998\par 00:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones Australia and New Zealand Report \par \uc2 DJAN\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--Australian bond prices are set to open lower Tuesday as most traders return to their desks after a three-day weekend to find the Australian dollar below US$0.6000 and heading lower. \par \par \uc2  Also, U.S. Treasury prices won't provide any support after ending their New York session near steady. \par \par \uc2  In New York Monday, benchmark 10-year Treasury notes finished at 5.558%, down from 5.562% Friday. \par \par \uc2  After rallying on Friday despite a strong U.S. employment report, buying interest has waned in U.S. Treasurys for the time being, traders said. They noted that caution now prevails ahead of U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Alan Greenspan's appearance Wednesday before the Joint Economic Committee of Congress. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, local traders last had an opportunity to adjust positions late Friday during overnight computerized trading. \par \par \uc2  In overnight trading Friday in Australia, March 10-year bond futures finished at 94.500, down 0.010, while three-year bond contracts closed at 94.80, down 0.02. September bank bill futures ended at 94.75, down 0.05. \par \par \uc2  A trader at a European investment bank said the weaker Australian dollar and soaring U.S. dollar "is the only story in town" Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  touched a new near 12-year low of US$0.5954 overnight despite rumored Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  early Monday. \par \par \uc2  He said fears of an interest-rate rise by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  would continue to push local bond prices lower Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  He noted that September bank bill futures prices have so far factored in just 20 basis points of an interest rate cut. As rate-rise fears grows, he said traders will move to factor in at least a full 50-basis-point rise. \par \par \uc2  The weaker local market will push the spread between U.S. yields and Australian yields back into positive territory, he added. The spread between benchmark U.S. and Australian 10-year yields has closed as low as -22 basis points. The spread is now around zero. \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, the only economic data due Tuesday is Australia & New Zealand Banking Group Ltd.'s job vacancy index for May. \par \par \uc2  -By Iain McDonald;61-2-9290-8828;imcdonald@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 08-06-98 \par \par \uc2  2210GMT \par \par \uc2  22765 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djan000020010916du68001j0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
