\par\par \b \uc2  U.S. Funds/A$ -2: Slumps Despite Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 09:02\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Also undermining the Australian dollar are worries that the fall-out from Asia's economic crisis will prompt a slowdown in the world economy that will cut into demand for commodities, Bowmer said. The losers then, are those commodity-based \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , like the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar's slump has occurred despite repeated \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the last 24 hours. Some dealers maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought between A$2.00 billion and A$3.00 billion in defense of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although one trader was skeptical about these estimates, suggesting the amount purchased was likely much smaller. \par \par \uc2  According to Whitley, the selling has been "purely profit-driven." \par \par \uc2  He suggested that U.S. hedge funds "attacked most of the Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 " with not a great deal of success," due mainly to poor liquidity in these markets. \par \par \uc2  Consequently, speculators have "turned their attention to the Australian dollar market, and to a lesser extent, the New Zealand dollar," which are relatively more liquid. \par \par \uc2  Whitley added that investors generally anticipate "it will be a long time before things start to improve" in Asia. \par \par \uc2  The Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained a downward trend since March 1997, although losses intensified from mid-1997 onward, mainly due to concern about the spill-over effects of Asia's economic crisis on the domestic economy. \par \par \uc2  These include a soft outlook for gold and commodity prices, a sharp deterioration of Australia's current-account deficit, and the potential for a further cut in Australian interest rates if domestic growth slows significantly. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0702GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6504tmv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
