\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Weaker Midmorning, Market Watchful For RBA \b0\par\par\uc2 327 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 03:05\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar remains weaker midmorning Friday, after failing to sustain overnight gains built on Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0045 GMT, the Australian dollar is quoted at US$0.6096, below US$0.6109 locally late Thursday. It also is at Y84.52, above Y84.45 Thursday, while the trade-weighted index has slipped to 56.5 from 56.6. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar is stalled nervously in a narrow US$0.6090-US$0.6100 range in morning dealings Friday. \par \par \uc2  This follows the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide to a near 12-year low of US$0.6068 in London overnight, before \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  drove the Australian dollar up to US$0.6157. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  couldn't sustain this rally, however, having slid back under US$0.6100 by late New York trading. The Australian dollar's retreat was fueled by a weaker New Zealand dollar on news that Moody's Investor Service placed New Zealand's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  debt and deposit ratings on review for possible downgrade. \par \par \uc2  According to dealers, the Reserve Bank of Australia bought on a couple of occasions during London trading, again during New York hours through the U.S. Federal Reserve, and in early local trading Friday around 2130 GMT. Dealers say the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has bought between A$2.00 billion and A$3.00 billion Australian dollars over the last 24 hours, at various levels between US$0.6075 and US$0.6155. \par \par \uc2  Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Ian Macfarlane in a speech at a business luncheon in London overnight confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in local trading Thursday, while a \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman Friday said he had no comment on reports of further \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Friday. \par \par \uc2  One U.S. bank dealer says that the Australian dollar "still looks pretty sick" Friday morning. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 05-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0105GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6504t8k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
