\par\par \b \uc2  CORRECTED - RBA at war with markets for besieged Australia. \b0\par\par\uc2 913 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 5 Juni 1998\par 05:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  In SYDNEY item "RBA at war with markets for besieged Australia dlr", please read the hedge fund profit in paragraph 14 as US$1 billion, thus correcting from one billion sterling. \par \par \uc2  A corrected repetition follows. \par \par \uc2  By Wayne Cole \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, June 5 (Reuters) - A desperate struggle is unfolding over the Australian dollar that could ultimately lead to a full blown \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  crisis and a rise in Australian interest rates. \par \par \uc2  "It's an Armageddon scenario," said David de Garis, senior Treasury analyst at ANZ. "The Reserve Bank may have to hike (rates) to stop the A$ becoming a casualty like the won or ringgit." \par \par \uc2  "The domestic fundamentals are not ringing any alarms, but the dollar surely is." \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) was forced to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively on Thursday to rescue the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from a 12-year low of 60.70 U.S. cents, as a who's who of U.S. investment banks and hedge funds dumped the dollar in massive amounts. \par \par \uc2  But the spending spree, which dealers estimated could have been as high as A$3.0 billion, bought only a brief breathing space and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was believed to be standing alone in the market on Friday buying at $0.6090. \par \par \uc2  Such was the pressure that RBA governor Ian Macfarlane took the unusual step of confirming the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in a speech in London, declaring the market had over reacted. \par \par \uc2  "A significant fall in the exchange rate as we have had was always going to be part of the adjustment to this external shock (from Asia), but an overshooting would be in no-one's interest," Macfarlane said. \par \par \uc2  The hapless \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been unhinged by Australia's trade exposure to a slowing Asia, which has already seen the country's current account deficit balloon by 33 percent in the first quarter. \par \par \uc2  Since last May, when the Asian crisis first grabbed headlines, the dollar has declined by no less than 16.5 U.S. cents or 21 percent, partly in response to this deterioration. The dollar has only been down at these levels once before, and then only briefly, when it plunged from around 67 cents in May to an all-time low around $0.5720 in July. \par \par \uc2  Macfarlane also took the opportunity to quash speculation of a rate cut here, saying an easing was very unlikely, and offered a stout defence of Australia's economic fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  But none of this seemed to carry much water with the heavyweight speculators in the U.S. \par \par \uc2  "Ever since the market forced sterling out of ERM back in 1992 it has reasoned that if it could roll the Bank of England then it could roll anyone," said a dealer at a local bank who wished to remain anonymous. \par \par \uc2  In 1992 world-wide selling of sterling forced it out of the Exchange Rate Mechanism of the European Monetary System despite all-out BoE \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and two hikes in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  One hedge fund alone, run by well-known speculator George Soros, made a US$1 billion profit from the debacle, and the profit-motive was clearly behind the local dollar's present difficulties. (corrects profit). \par \par \uc2  The latest target might seem even easier since the RBA's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserves are about half the BoE's at around A$20 billion, or US$12.2 billion, a sum any respectable hedge fund could raise with a few phone calls. \par \par \uc2  "The market will be quietly adding up what the RBA spends, waiting for it to run low on ammunition," said J.P. Morgan senior economist John Kyriakopoulos. \par \par \uc2  And spending it was, with dealers estimating at least A$1.0 billion, and perhaps as much as A$3.0 billion, changed hands in New York overnight. There was even talk the U.S. Federal Reserve had lent a hand and bought the A$ on its own account. The two. \par \par \uc2  central banks have a reciprocal agreement on \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders reported whispers one U.S. bank had sold A$600 miion in a single deal, with the lonely buyer supposedly the RBA. \par \par \uc2  Rory Robertson, a fixed income analyst at Bankers Trust Australia, noted the RBA had been prepared to put its reserves on the line in the past. \par \par \uc2  "We know that the last time they were concerned the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had overshot in the period between late 1991 and late 1993, they actually did A$18 billion of buying," he said. "So they do have a lot of money they're prepared to throw at it." \par \par \uc2  Whether this would be enough alone to stop the rot depended greatly on developments in Asia, which were still highly volatile. \par \par \uc2  "The worry is that if you get through this psychologically important 60 cent level, it can take you somewhere you do not want to be in terms of the inflation outlook," said Robertson. \par \par \uc2  The depreciation in the dollar had aready shown up in rising import prices which prompted the RBA to revise up expectations for inflation growth in the next year or so. \par \par \uc2  "We are getting to the point where the Reserve Bank would be pondering on the scenario in which they would be forced to raise rates," Robertson said. \par \par \uc2  "So it's clear the Reserve Bank's bias has shifted from easing to a tightening, although the chance of a hike is still very slim." \par \par \uc2  ((Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800, fax 61 2 9262-4727, sydney.newsroom @reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6503m2c\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
