\par\par \b \uc2  N.Y. Mid-Afternoon -2: Caution Ahead of Payroll Data \b0\par\par\uc2 397 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1998\par 21:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  reportedly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market Thursday in support of the Australian dollar, which had fallen to a new 12-year low against the dollar. \par \par \uc2  "The Aussie dollar is not out of the woods yet," said Alex Beuzelin, market analyst at Ruesche international in Washington, D.C. \par \par \uc2  Despite the aggressive move by the RBA, the market remains largely bullish on the Australian dollar, in large part due to the Asian contagion and Australia's ballooning current account deficit. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, traders also remain cautious ahead of Friday's release of crucial U.S. non-farm payroll report, which is expected to show the economy created 262,000 jobs in May. \par \par \uc2  Another factor keeping traders from taking large positions is next Tuesday's meeting in Paris of finance officials from the Group of Eight nations. \par \par \uc2  Although the official topic of the meeting will be Russia's troubles - a Japanese \b \highlight22\uc2 Ministry of Finance\b0 \highlight\uc2  source reportedly said \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  would not be on the agenda - the market remains somewhat wary of concerted market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in support of the yen. \par \par \uc2  The dollar has languished in a tight range since reaching a seven-year high late last week as bulls seek to take it above the psychologically important level of Y140. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par "There is no reason to be long of yen, no reason to be short of\par dollars," Lee Kassler, vice president at Israel Discount Bank of New\par York said. 