\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2 /RBA/Buying -3:  \highlight22\uc2 Intervened \highlight\uc2  Twice Thursday - Dealers \b0\par\par\uc2 258 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1998\par 12:29\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar was sharply lower late Thursday despite reports the Reserve Bank of Australia was in supporting the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  twice during the day. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the Australian dollar through brokers at US$0.6080, around midafternoon, prompting a quick rally in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a peak of around A$0.6129. \par \par \uc2  A trader who declined to be named said the Reserve Bank bought the Australian dollar again at US$0.6075 in early London trading, pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  above US$0.6100. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  spokesman said he had no comment to make on any \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  talk. \par \par \uc2  Late Thursday in London trade the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a low US$0.6068, its lowest level reached since September 1986, before recovering on the reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. \par \par \uc2  At 1015 GMT, the Australian dollar was changing hands at US$0.6105, down from US$0.6163 late in Sydney Wednesday. It also was at Y84.43, below Y84.86 Wednesday, while the trade-weighted index slipped to 56.6 from 56.7. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar has fallen two U.S. cents from a US$0.6280 peak touched last Friday to Thursday's low. \par \par \uc2  Weighing on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been a host of negative factors, including soft gold and commodity prices, concern about an expected deterioration of Australia's current-account deficit over 1998, a generally weak yen and lingering speculation about a further cut in interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 04-06-98 \par \par \uc2  1029GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6404s5j\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
