\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr/RBA -3: After Failure To Benefit From Data \b0\par\par\uc2 328 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1998\par 07:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying followed the Australian dollar's slide to a US$0.6080 low during in the session, its lowest level reached since September 1986. \par \par \uc2  A European bank trader said the Australian dollar had been hit early afternoon by a large sell order out of Asia. When Australian banks moved to cover short positions left over from that sell order, they found the Reserve Bank on the bid side through the brokers. \par \par \uc2  The trader added that the Australian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had "traded like a dog all day", while "price action has been very poor." \par \par \uc2  According to the trader, market participants had decided that the potential for another bout of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying had increased after the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to benefit from a series of positive economic figures released over the last week, including a higher-than-expected 1.3% first-quarter rise in gross domestic product announced Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The trader said he hadn't expected the Reserve Bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  Thursday, as the decline in the Australian dollar had been orderly, and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Ian Macfarlane is due to speak in London later Thursday. \par \par \uc2  A local bank dealer agreed that trading Thursday had been "one-sided". However, with little in the way of fresh fundamental news to justify the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide Thursday, the dealer said he wasn't that surprised to see the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  step in to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has previously indicated that it is more likely to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar when trading is deemed not to be "orderly." \par \par \uc2  Dealers say a host of factors have weighed on the Australian dollar recently, including soft gold and commodity prices, a generally weak yen, concern about a deterioration of Australia's current-account deficit over 1998, and still lingering speculation about a further cut in domestic interest rates. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 04-06-98 \par \par \uc2  0555GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du6404rkl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
