\par\par \b \uc2  RBA chief says Australia battered by Asian crisis. \b0\par\par\uc2 348 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Juni 1998\par 18:05\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LONDON, June 4 (Reuters) - Australia's links to troubled Asian economies have damaged the country's export markets but the worst may be over, Reserve Bank governor Ian Macfarlane said on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "It is definitely hurting us at the moment," Macfarlane said in a speech in London, adding that the downward pressure on exports and the Aussie dollar had led the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up its ailing \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "A significant fall (in the Aussie) would always be part of the impact, but an overshooting would be in no one's interest," Macfarlane said. \par \par \uc2  Speculation swirled in London and New York markets earlier over \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , both by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) and the U.S. Federal Reserve. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman at the Federal Reserve Bank of New York declined to comment on the market rumours, which came amid a bounce in the Aussie to a day high of $0.6154. \par \par \uc2  But a spokesman for the RBA confirmed that the bank had supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "All I can tell you is that yes we have been \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  today and I cannot give you any more colour on that," a source at the RBA said. \par \par \uc2  Australia's trade exposure to the battered Asian region has seen the country's current account deficit rise 33 percent in the first quarter of this year. \par \par \uc2  Yet in assessing the future prospects for Asia and Australia, Macfarlane held out hope that the worst of the crisis had been already seen. \par \par \uc2  "I think it's probably fair to say that we are already in the period of maximum contractionary events," he said. \par \par \uc2  Macfarlane noted that the country's export industries were finding other outlets for their goods, and said there had been no deterioration in its trade with Japan. \par \par \uc2  Regarding Japan's future economic performance, Macfarlane said he expected a slight improvement. \par \par \uc2  "Next year will look a lot better for Japan but it won't be anything to write home about," he added. \par \par \uc2  (London newsroom +44 171 542 7770)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du6403hti\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
