\par\par \b \uc2  INSIGHT-Aussie dollar slithers on weak yen, gold. \b0\par\par\uc2 477 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1998\par 00:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  ---------------------------------------------------------------- \par \par \uc2  AUS$ S/Term range  *Support *Restnce *RSI-14 *MA-10  *MA-20 \par \par \uc2  US$ *0.6175/0.6250 *0.6200  *0.6230  * 30.00 *0.6258 *0.6321 \par \par \uc2  --------------VIEWS FROM THE MARKET - May 27 ------------------- \par \par \uc2      * Overnight range roughly $0.6210/$0.6244 \par \par \uc2      * Australian dollar slides overnight on weak yen and \par \par \uc2  slippage in commodities prices, as London and New York return \par \par \uc2  from holiday weekend. \par \par \uc2      * Retest of $0.6170 low of May 18 seen likely in coming \par \par \uc2  days, with little standing in the way of further losses. \par \par \uc2       * Second-tier data including wage trends due out Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, May 27 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar slithered lower overnight under pressure from a soft yen and falling commodity prices, paving the way for a renewed test of last week's US$0.6170 low. \par \par \uc2  Steady selling pressure as London and New York returned from holiday weekends gathered pace as gold fell and the Commodities Research Bureau index fell to fresh two-year lows. \par \par \uc2  By 8.25 am (2225 GMT), a suffering dollar was clinging to support at 62 U.S. cents, trading at US$0.6203/08, well below its $0.6234/39 here late on Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Technical analysts said the next support level was seen at $0.6170, the 11-year low reached last week that prompted a rare \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Below that, the view was wide open to as low as 60 US cents. \par \par \uc2  The RBA was believed to be more concerned by the speed of the decline than the actual level, and any further sudden slippage could elicit further buying by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Weighing on the dollar overnight was a US$4.40 drop in Comex June gold to $295.60 an ounce, and a slide in the CRB index of a hefty 3.21 points or 1.46 percent to 215.92. \par \par \uc2  The weakness in commodity prices compounded the already substantial pressure on the Aussie from a weak yen. \par \par \uc2  The yen gained a temporary reprieve after U.S. Treasury Secretary Robert Rubin said he was surprised by an article that said he would not mind a weaker yen. The yen strengthened to 136.98 to the dollar, helping the Aussie move up to $0.6235, before weakening again by late New York trade to around 137.80, and taking the local dollar lower with it. \par \par \uc2  The negative sentiment on the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was compounded by comments from Moody's Investors Service that New Zealand's current account deficit was a source of concern. \par \par \uc2  On the data front, the Westpac Leading Index for March and wage trends in enterprise bargaining for the first quarter are expected to have no impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , with all eyes firmly on regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Victoria Thieberger, Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800, sydney.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5q04g0l\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
