\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Modestly Lower Late; Focus On Indonesia \b0\par\par\uc2 343 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1998\par 08:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar was modestly lower versus the U.S. dollar late Wednesday, having stalled in range-trading over the local session while traders kept a wary eye on Indonesia. \par \par \uc2  At 0620 GMT, the Australian dollar was quoted at US$0.6242, down from US$0.6253 locally late Tuesday. It also was at Y85.15, above Y84.81 Tuesday, while the trade-weighted index slipped to 57.3 from 57.6. \par \par \uc2  The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  saw steadier trading Wednesday, stalled in a US$0.6221-US$0.6245 range. This followed the Australian dollar's climb from a near 12-year low at US$0.6173 to US$0.6275 Tuesday, after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The Australian dollar had been under pressure from instability in Indonesia, and weaker gold and commodity prices. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  traded with a cautious tone early Wednesday ahead of planned anti-government demonstrations in Indonesia. However, after key Indonesian opposition leader Amien Rais canceled the planned nationwide protest Wednesday morning, regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  took on a steadier tone. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said the continued presence of U.S. fund selling interest helped temper the Australian dollar's topside Wednesday, while traders were wary of testing lower levels given the possibility of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar was unaffected by news late morning that the Westpac Banking Corp./Melbourne Institute's consumer sentiment index rose 0.9% in May. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par Moving into the overnight session, John Radinoff, executive director\par of \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 foreign exchange\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  at SBC Warburg Australia ltd. said that the\par Australian dollar likely will continue to consolidate for the moment, in\par the absence of fresh news out of Asia. He noted that there are sell\par orders initially toward US$0.6250, including U.S. fund selling interest,\par while stop-loss sell orders are sighted under US$0.6200.\par    -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 20-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 0640GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5k048zr\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
