\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Lower Vs U.S. Dlr Midmorning; Indonesia Eyed \b0\par\par\uc2 322 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Mai 1998\par 01:47\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar is lower versus the U.S. dollar midmorning Wednesday, although the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has taken on a steadier tone following Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  At 2340 GMT, the Australian dollar is quoted at US$0.6229, down from US$0.6253 locally late Tuesday. It also is at Y84.95, above Y84.81 Tuesday, while the trade-weighted index has eased to 57.5 from 57.6. \par \par \uc2  In dealings overnight, the Australian dollar dipped to a US$0.6212 low as the U.S. dollar strengthened versus the yen, according to one analyst. However, after the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting resulted in no change to monetary policy, the yen regained some ground which also help lift the Australian dollar off its lows, the analyst adds. \par \par \uc2  There is little on the domestic front to offer direction Wednesday which should see attention focused on Indonesia, where anti-government rallies are planned Wednesday. Dealers caution that renewed violence in Indonesia likely will see the rupiah, and in turn other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , under pressure. \par \par \uc2  A couple of dealers say the fact that the market is already short-positioned, and nervousness about further Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  should provide some support for the Australian dollar in the near term, while ongoing U.S.-based selling interest is seen tempering gains. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar early Tuesday, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell to a near 12-year low of US$0.6173. According to dealers, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought Australian dollars around US$0.6200, and again near US$0.6250/US$0.6260. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par The analyst suggests an intra day range for the Australian dollar\par Wednesday of U$0.6190-US$0.6250.\par    --By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-05-98\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 2347GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5j04b5o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
