\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr -2: Mkt Seen Vulnerable To Short-Squeeze \b0\par\par\uc2 304 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 09:22\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Dealers said that to the extent market participants view Suharto as largely responsible for the state of affairs in Indonesia, news that the current Indonesian leader won't seek reelection is positive for the Asian region. And while Australia is lumped in with its Asian neighbors, the news is also supportive of the Australian dollar, dealers added. \par \par \uc2  A National Australia Bank dealer said U.S. buying emerged soon after Suharto's comments, and prompted a bout of short-covering on the Australian dollar late afternoon. \par \par \uc2  Moving into the overnight session, the market is very much aware of reported strong U.S.-based selling interest sighted at US$0.6270 earlier Tuesday, the dealer said. While this leaves traders cautious of testing the topside, with the market largely short-positioned, a short-squeeze can't be ruled out, he commented. \par \par \uc2  On the downside, the dealer doesn't anticipate the Australian dollar will retest its overnight lows in the near term, given wariness about further Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Geoff Bowmer, vice president of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Bankers Trust Australia Ltd., agreed that the "market is susceptible to a short-squeeze." \par \par \uc2  Bowmer said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying Tuesday appeared to hold a more aggressive tone than merely "testing and calming" the market. \par \par \uc2  Bowmer also didn't rule out further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  "if further Asian difficulties" prompt renewed Australian dollar weakness. He added that the Reserve Bank mightn't necessarily wait until the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  dipped under US$0.6200 before stepping in again. \par \par \uc2  On the topside, Bowmer said initial resistance lies at US$0.6280, a break of which would target US$0.6310. \par \par \uc2  -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0722GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5j048qg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
