\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Stronger At Midday But Off Morning Highs \b0\par\par\uc2 390 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 04:52\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar is stronger at midsession Tuesday, although off morning highs reached after the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 0240 GMT, the Australian dollar is quoted at US$0.6248, up from US$0.6229 locally late Monday. It also is at Y84.93, above Y84.21 Monday, while the trade-weighted index has risen to 57.9 from 57.4. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar touched a US$0.6275 high in early trading Tuesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  According to dealers, the amount involved in the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  was difficult to determine given that the buying was through the brokers. However, one dealer estimates the Reserve Bank bought around A$200.0 million and A$300.0 million. Dealers suggest the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bought the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  around US$0.6200 and again at US$0.6250/US$0.6260. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 -led rally followed a dip to a new near 12-year low at US$0.6173 overnight. Dealers blamed ongoing concern about instability in Indonesia, a sharp drop in commodity prices and a stronger U.S. dollar versus the yen for the Australian dollar's overnight decline. \par \par \uc2  In dealings Tuesday morning the Australian dollar has eased back from its early high to touch a US$0.6237 late-morning low. Dealers say solid U.S. name selling near US$0.6270 tempered the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rally, while renewed weakness amongst the Southeast Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  also is weighing on the Australian dollar Tuesday. \par \par \uc2  Ongoing concern about events in Indonesia sees traders nervously awaiting details of an address by Indonesian President Suharto to the nation, scheduled to begin at 0200 GMT. In particular, traders are on watch for any indication Suharto might announce his resignation. \par \par \uc2  A couple of dealers say initial support for the Australian dollar lies at US$0.6230, a break of which target's the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's overnight low of US$0.6173, and will see traders wary of further \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Resistance is eyed at US$0.6280/US$0.6290. \par \par \uc2  -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 19-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0252GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 2766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5j047r0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
