\par\par \b \uc2  RBA confirms it  \highlight22\uc2 intervened \highlight\uc2  to buy Australian dlr. \b0\par\par\uc2 141 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 01:13\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, May 19 (Reuters) - The Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier on Tuesday to buy Australian dollars. \par \par \uc2  "We can confirm that the reports of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  are correct," the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said. \par \par \uc2  It would not say what levels it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  at, however. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the RBA looked to have \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the local dollar broke beneath 62 U.S. cents overnight to reach a 12 year low around $0.6173. \par \par \uc2  The buying was enough to lift the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to $0.6270 where it steadied. \par \par \uc2  The RBA last overtly \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on January 9 this year when it bought around A$100 million at $0.6320 in a bid to prevent the dollar's decline from becoming disorderly. \par \par \uc2  ((Sydney newsroom, 61-2 9373 1800, sydney.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5i05350\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
