\par\par \b \uc2  Australian dlr extends slide, hits near 12-yr low. \b0\par\par\uc2 180 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1998\par 21:10\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2      NEW YORK, May 18 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar fell beneath the key $0.6200 level on Monday as concerns over the festering Asian crisis sapped confidence in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said. \par \par \uc2     Stop-loss selling was triggered at the $0.6200 level, sending the Aussie as low as $0.6175, a fresh 12-year low. \par \par \uc2  Steep losses in the yen against the dollar and the mark exacerbated sales of the Australian dollar, which retreated in late U.S. trade from a weak bounce earlier, said Russell LaScala, head of spot trading at Citibank. \par \par \uc2  LaScala noted that the Aussie slide would be met with some caution in anticipation of possible \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . History shows that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  (RBA) has been highly effective in previous \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , he said. \par \par \uc2  "Right now you don't want to step in front of the trend, which is much lower, but any speak from the RBA and I'd be bottom fishing," he added. \par \par \uc2  ((N.A. Treasury Desk, 212-859-1672)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5i052y5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
