\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Higher Early After RBA  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rumors \b0\par\par\uc2 186 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Mai 1998\par 00:04\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--The Australian dollar is higher early Tuesday following rumors that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 2150 GMT, the Australian dollar is quoted at US$0.6260, up from US$0.6229 locally late Monday. It also is at Y84.96, above Y84.21 Monday. \par \par \uc2  The Australian dollar remained under pressure overnight, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sliding to a US$0.6173 low, its lowest level reached in nearly 12 years, according to one local bank dealer. \par \par \uc2  However, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  quickly reversed its position in early Australasian trading Tuesday as rumors that the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prompted a quick rebound to a high so far of US$0.6274. \par \par \uc2  According to the dealer, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is thought to have bought Australian dollars near US$0.6200 and again around US$0.6250. \par \par \uc2  A spokesman for the Reserve Bank of Australia said he couldn't comment on the rumors. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) Dow Jones Newswires 18-05-98 \par \par \uc2  2204GMT \par \par \uc2  1054 22766 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5i04760\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
