\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr/Near 12-Yr Low Late -3: US$0.6200 Key Level \b0\par\par\uc2 242 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Mai 1998\par 08:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Looking ahead, Australian dollar risk is likely to remain weighted to the downside while Asian-related uncertainty lingers, according to dealers. \par \par \uc2  O'Leary said that a move below US$0.6200 would be notably bearish for the Australian dollar, although in anticipation of that, he expects the Australian dollar will be well-defended between US$0.6200 and US$0.6210. \par \par \uc2  On the topside, O'Leary sees the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  capped toward US$0.6290 overnight. He added that U.S. sellers continue to emerge on any local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  rallies. \par \par \uc2  There has been no talk of the Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the Australian dollar as yet, although with the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  near 12-year lows, traders remain on watch for the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's presence. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the Australian dollar during the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's dive to a then near-12-year low at US$0.6315 in January. At that time, the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's slide was fueled by panic-selling related to the rupiah's fall. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par However, analysts say that while the Australian dollar's slide is\par based on orderly trading, and involves good two-way dealings, the\par \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 central bank\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  is unlikely to step in to support the Australian dollar.\par   