\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr/Late -2: Focus On Asian Mkts To Continue \b0\par\par\uc2 306 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 Mai 1998\par 09:32\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Next week, "potentially significant from a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market perspective, will be developments in Asia, particularly Indonesia," commented Commonwealth Bank of Australia economists Michael Blythe and David Moore in a weekly report. "Further instability in the region would see the Australian dollar under further pressure in the near term." \par \par \uc2  Looking further ahead, Citibank ltd. economists Stephen Koukoulas and Annette Beacher said in a report Friday that they maintain a near-term bearish outlook on the Australian dollar, and couldn't rule out an "overshoot" to US$0.6000-US$0.6100. \par \par \uc2  According to Citibank, factors weighing on the Australian dollar include "a likely easing in (domestic) monetary policy, soft commodity prices, some still bad news on the trade and current-account front and further U.S. dollar strength." \par \par \uc2  The Citibank economists suggested that "the short position of the market, plus some rumored Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may put a floor under the Australian dollar at some stage." \par \par \uc2  Colonial State Bank chief economist Craig James said Friday that the Australian dollar is now in "over-sold territory. The further it falls, the more we need to be wary of a bounce-back." \par \par \uc2  While it might be too soon to talk about a rebound, James cautioned that on three occasions in the last 13 years, the Australian dollar has bounced back by over US 6 cents within a four-month period. According to James, "factors to watch (that might provide a boost to the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) include a change of government in Indonesia, permanent tax cuts in Japan, a drop in base metal inventories and a stronger gold price due to higher-than-expected gold holdings by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." \par \par \uc2  -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 15-05-98 \par \par \uc2  0732GMT \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010916du5f044g3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
