\par\par \b \uc2  Australian Dlr Late -2: Mkt Eying U.S. Dlr Trading Vs Yen \b0\par\par\uc2 228 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 9 Januar 1998\par 07:46\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1998, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  According to Aggar, Australian dollar direction remains tied to U.S. dollar trading versus the yen. \par \par \uc2  He said that the market remains 'very nervous and spooked' after Friday's reported \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and amid ongoing Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  turmoil. \par \par \uc2  Moving into the overnight session, Aggar suggested that should the U.S. dollar continue its decline versus the yen, the Australian dollar might well edge up toward US$0.6450. On the downside, he said US$0.6315/US$0.6320, which represents the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's intra day lows, should prove to be a key support area. \par \par \uc2  'The Australian dollar is expected to face another turbulent time over the coming week,' commented Craig James, chief economist at Colonial State Bank. \par \par \uc2  James warned that 'rumors of Reserve Bank (of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets may be more commonplace if the Australian dollar shows renewed downside momentum to US$0.6300.' \par \par \uc2  Commonwealth Bank of Australia economists Michael Blythe and David Thurtell, in a weekly outlook, said that while the fall out from Asia suggests further weakness for the Australian dollar, 'Reserve Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , rumored and actual, might put a bit of backbone in the Australian dollar next week.' \par \par \uc2  -By Sandra Muldoon; 612-9290-8871; smuldoon@ap.org \par \par \uc2  (END) Dow Jones Newswires 09-01-98 \par \par 