\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2  dlr leaps on rumours of RBA  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 581 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Januar 1998\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SYDNEY, Jan 9 (Reuters) - The Australian dollar jumped 3/4 cent in confused trading on Friday as a big buy order went through, sparking rumours the Reserve Bank had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been testing key support around $0.6320/25 this morning having slipped from $0.6365/70 late on Thursday, but suddenly leapt to $0.6380 in a single bound. Traders said a local bank had been on the bid but they could not be certain if it was acting for a private customer or the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The talk is of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but we didn't see the flows and cannot confirm it," said one dealer at another local bank. By 10.00 a.m. (2300 GMT) the rally had extended to $0.6406/11. \par \par \uc2  A Reserve Bank spokesman said the bank's policy was never to comment on market rumours or its \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Dealers emphasised that it could as easily be a speculator buying large in the hope of sparking just such talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which would turn into a self-fulfilling stop-loss rally. If so, the buyer could be expected to bail out once he had made a decent profit, and the A$ would drift lower. \par \par \uc2  But if it was the RBA taking a stand then the outlook for the dollar could have changed significantly. Up to now the A$ has been seen as a riskless selling opportunity by speculators since it was assumed the RBA was comfortable with its decline. \par \par \uc2  In a testimony to a Parliamentary banking committee back in November RBA governor Ian Macfarlane said the fall in the dollar up to then had been a reasonable reaction to the troubles brewing in Australia's key Asian export markets. \par \par \uc2  At that time the dollar had fallen around five cents from when the Asian crisis began back in July to stand at $0.7050. Since then the troubles had engulfed Korea as well and the market had assumed the RBA would be content to see the dollar depreciate further to compensate. \par \par \uc2  Many had noted the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was steady in trade weighted terms, so reducing the inflation threat from a lower A$/US$. \par \par \uc2  Nevertheless, analysts said the dollar had depreciated on an import weighted basis, which is what mattered for inflation, and would contribute to prices rising this year, possibly toward the top of the RBA's 2-3 percent target band. \par \par \uc2  The last time the bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in any serious manner was in 1993 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was also down close to 64 cents, but in that case the TWI had also tumbled to hit record lows and there was a real risk of imported inflation. \par \par \uc2  Dealers said there was the possibility the RBA had bought for its own portfolio reasons rather than as a protest about the dollar's low level. \par \par \uc2  They noted the bank had been selling dollars for portfolio reasons in late 1996 and early 1997 when it had been up around 80 cents and made a considerable profit in the process. \par \par \uc2  It would thus be reasonable for the bank, which has a very long time horizon for investment, to be buying dollars now when the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was close to historic lows. \par \par \uc2  Whatever the facts, the rumour would be enough to make bears more cautious in future and dealers saw scope to re-test Wednesday's $0.6450 high in the short term. \par \par \uc2  -- Wayne Cole 61-2 9373 1800 \par \par \uc2  (c) Reuters Limited 1998 \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010926du18019rn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
