\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Australia \highlight\uc2  RBA Governor: Didn't  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  To Help A$ Past Yr \b0\par\par\uc2 250 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 August 1997\par 17:45\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1997, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SYDNEY (Dow Jones)--Reserve Bank of Australia Governor Ian Macfarlane said Tuesday the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market "in the past year" to support the value of the Australian dollar. \par \par \uc2  In addressing a gathering of company directors in Perth, the central banker was asked about the Reserve Bank's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the support of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "We haven't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Macfarlane replied, "to hold the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  up." \par \par \uc2  In about a month, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is slated to issue an annual report for fiscal year 1996-97, ended June 30. In its annual reports, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  normally sketches its \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  over the financial year. Macfarlane foreshadowed some of that detail for fiscal year 1996-97 by saying: "we \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  earlier in the year, but we were buying back reserves." \par \par \uc2  Additionally, he told the group that the only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has done "in the past 18 months has had the effect of pushing the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  down." \par \par \uc2  In fiscal year 1995-96, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  undertook some purchases of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  for its own accounts, as well. It said in that annual report that "these purchases were not intended to influence the exchange rate, but to facilitate a further run-off of outstanding swaps accumulated during 1992 and 1993 when the (\b \highlight22\uc2 central) bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  heavily to support the Australian dollar." \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS  08-12-97 \par \par \uc2  1145EDT \par \par \uc2  4012 4340 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011006dt8c01puc\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
