\par\par \b \uc2  World  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  -3: Rumors Of BOJ  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  Help Dlr Vs JPY \b0\par\par\uc2 298 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 2 August 1996\par 23:08\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1996, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  The dollar initially made gains against the yen early in Asian dealings as unconfirmed rumors circulated that the Bank of Japan (BOJ) was \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support a falling dollar. \par \par \uc2  The dollar first shot up to its intraday high of 107.25 yen at 0418 GMT from 106.75 yen around 0330 GMT when rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was in the market began to circulate. \par \par \uc2  'The dollar moved higher against the yen with the fact that perhaps we did or didn't see BOJ \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ,' said National \b \highlight22\uc2 Australia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Sakamoto. 'But the fact that the market is fearing (possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) around the 106.50 yen level means you don't want to be caught short dollars down there. Right now, the dollar is happy at about 0.25 percentage points on either side of 107.00 yen.' \par \par \uc2  The dollar continued erratic trading against the yen throughout much of the global day, as it seemed supported, whether by the BOJ or not, around 106.75 yen and capped around the 107.20 yen level by heavy selling pressure, traders said. \par \par \uc2  Sterling also dropped against most major \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , as traders cited large orders to sell sterling for marks but especially for yen. \par \par \uc2  At the close of global trading, sterling was quoted at 2.2768 marks, down from 2.2918 marks late Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Some dealers attributed sterling's decline to a break of a key technical support level at 164.90 yen. Others cited warnings from the European Union Commission that the lifting of the export bank on British beef might be delayed by reports that so-called mad cow disease may be passed on by cows to their calves. \par \par \uc2  (MORE) AP-DOW JONES NEWS 02-08-96 \par \par \uc2  2108GMT \par \par \uc2  1033 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020011013ds8206b64\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
