\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Australia Central Bank \highlight\uc2  -5-: No  \highlight22\uc2 Forex \highlight\uc2  Market  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 212 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Oktober 1995\par 07:35\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 1995, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  Addressing other topics, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said capacity constraints aren't expected to intensify over the next year, and might even ease a bit more. \par \par \uc2  Cost pressures from the labor market are likely to remain, but they might partly be offset by lower price increases for other inputs, particularly imported inputs, the Reserve Bank said. \par \par \uc2  On a separate topic, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it didn't undertake any \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  during the third quarter of 1995. It noted that it hasn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on either side of the market for almost two years. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did, however, make some purchases in the market to fund the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs of the government. \par \par \uc2  In the third quarter, the Reserve Bank purchased the equivalent of $454 million (Australian) of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to replenish \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold to the government. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  noted that it has resumed this "usual" practice of acquiring foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the market as necessary to meet government needs after a hiatus of several years. \par \par \uc2  In the last few years, the government's \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  needs have been met from the proceeds of its own foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  swap program. \par \par \uc2  (END) DOW JONES NEWS 10-18-95 \par \par \uc2  0135EDT \par \par \uc2  4012 4160 4216 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020011024drai02dnd\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
